Let $matbold(A) = (a_(i j))$. The $i$th column is $matbold(A) vb(e_i)$. If $matbold(A) in O(n)$, these columns have pairwise dot products $delta_(i j)$, so they form an orthonormal basis. The orthonormal-column condition gives
$
  (matbold(A) vb(e_i))^TT (matbold(A) vb(e_j)) = delta_(i j),
$
which is equivalent to $matbold(A)^TT matbold(A) = matbold(I)_n$. Conversely, that matrix equation gives $(matbold(A) vb(u)) dot (matbold(A) vb(v)) = vb(u) dot vb(v)$, so $matbold(A) in O(n)$.
